#### African Drumming Incursions for Schools

Our African drumming incursions bring students together through the power of rhythm. Every student has the opportunity to play a West African drum, learn rhythmic patterns and contribute to a group musical experience.

Students are introduced to traditional West African rhythms and explore the sounds and techniques of instruments such as the djembe. Through practical activities, rhythm games and call-and-response exercises, they learn to listen, find the beat and work together to create an exciting rhythmic ensemble.

No previous drumming experience is necessary. Our facilitators guide students through the rhythms step by step, making the experience accessible to beginners while providing opportunities to develop musical skills and coordination.

African drumming workshops encourage students to listen to one another, take turns, follow cues and contribute to a shared outcome. The result is an energetic, hands-on music experience that gets the whole group involved.

