## School Incursion Experience

 Rhythm Culture has delivered drumming, singing and dance activities to schools and educational organisations in the Sunshine Coast and Australia-wide since 2011.

 Our school incursion history includes performing arts activities at Pinnacle Academic College, a Year 12 retreat at Stuartholme School in the Sunshine Coast Hinterland and drumming and dancing incursions for [Kawana Waters State College](https://kawanawaterssc.eq.edu.au/), [Pacific Lutheran College](https://www.pacificlutheran.qld.edu.au/), [Sunshine Coast Grammar School](https://www.scgs.qld.edu.au/), [Immanuel Lutheran College](https://www.immanuel.qld.edu.au/), [Nambour Christian College](https://www.ncc.qld.edu.au/), [Glasshouse Christian College](https://glasshouse.qld.edu.au/), [Meriden State College](https://meridansc.eq.edu.au/), [Good Shepherd Lutheran College](https://www.gslc.qld.edu.au/), [Coolum Beach Christian College,](https://www.cbcc.qld.edu.au/) [St Andrews Christian College](https://www.saac.qld.edu.au/), [Maleny State School](https://malenyss.eq.edu.au/), [Woombye State School](https://woombyess.eq.edu.au/), [Caloundra State School](https://caloundrass.eq.edu.au/) and drum and dance activities for school and vacation-care programs.

 These experiences reflect the flexibility of our workshops, from focused student groups and retreats to larger events where students can rotate through different performing arts activities.

 We bring practical experience in facilitating group music and movement, helping students participate in an engaging shared experience.

If you're planning an upcoming school event, get in touch to discuss your requirements and how Rhythm Culture could contribute.

